# Projects — the rule that matters

Work happens in a **project**. Thalos is the default, the world being
discovered. Earth is the **fixture**: a known planet so shaping can be
tested on a base whose tectonics we already know. Earth is not a tree —
no search, no variants, no seed to shuffle.

**Artifacts belong to a variant**, not to a project or a seed:
`preview/<project>/v/<id>/`. Loading another project or variant must not
show the last one's tiles.

**Loading a project assigns the authored bag, never merges it** —
otherwise a knob the new file does not name keeps the last value and the
planet belongs to neither.

Do not treat the generator's Earth-calibrated `DEFAULTS` as a third
project. Those are the unmarked baseline the body sits on.

How the studio works: [docs/studio.md](../../docs/studio.md). Language:
